         writes < 1 rad between frames a distance xi_F = 0.5 apart
    optical photon 500 nm, 1 m lab arm           : P needed  8.89e-91 -> l_k ~  1.29e-15 m  (l = 7.96e-08 m)
    optical photon 500 nm, 1 Gpc (quasar/GRB)    : P needed 2.88e-116 -> l_k ~  5.95e-10 m  (l = 7.96e-08 m)
    radio 21 cm, 1 Gpc                           : P needed 1.63e-127 -> l_k ~  1.88e-07 m  (l = 3.34e-02 m)
    gamma 1 GeV (1.24e-15 m), 1 Gpc              : P needed  4.68e-99 -> l_k ~  8.90e-14 m  (l = 1.97e-16 m)
    electron, tau = 1 ns (biprism)               : P needed  1.26e-79 -> l_k ~  4.28e-18 m  (lambda_C = 3.86e-13 m)
    neutron, tau = 0.1 ms (crystal interferometer): P needed  4.25e-78 -> l_k ~  1.96e-18 m  (lambda_C = 2.10e-16 m)
    Cs-133 atom, 70 s (sum over 133 nucleons)    : P needed  4.56e-86 -> l_k ~  1.16e-16 m  (lambda_C = 2.10e-16 m)
    25 kDa molecule, 7 ms (sum over nucleons)    : P needed  2.43e-84 -> l_k ~  4.78e-17 m  (lambda_C = 2.10e-16 m)

comparator (Pikovski et al. 2015 mechanism): branch phase-rate difference per unit rest energy = g dx/c^2 = 1.09e-22 (dx = 1 um);
  here (B2) per unit rest energy and unit frame distance = 3 R_lC, e.g. nucleon at a=l_P, flat L=4 kernel: 3.90e+54
